                                "sense_id": "5509dd7a-c731-3a71-8efb-69d4ec9406e9",
                                "text": "And men themselves contented well with plaine and simple foode, That on the earth by natures gift without their travell stoode, Did live by raspis ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4388c7a8-1106-44fe-a834-f78a7aa3a306",
                                "sense_id": "5509dd7a-c731-3a71-8efb-69d4ec9406e9",
                                "text": "It were good to keepe some of the juyce of raspis-berries in some wooden vessel, and to make it, as it were, raspis wine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "687c67e0-3a5b-40dd-a0c7-86f3ac7f5a0c",
                                "sense_id": "5509dd7a-c731-3a71-8efb-69d4ec9406e9",
                                "text": "In this manner you may preserve Raspices and Mulberries."
